# Design system (Cursor)

Operational constraints while implementing in this repo. Canonical policy: `AGENTS.md`. Do not invent tokens or component behavior.

## Figma MCP

- Inspect the file, variables/collections, and component conventions before create or edit
- Reuse existing structures; do not recreate tokens or components that already exist
- Inspect Figma before changing it
- On Figma↔code disagreement: report first; do not choose a winner silently

## Tokens

- Consume semantic tokens; never hardcode product colors (e.g. `bg-blue-500`) when a semantic token exists
- Edit `tokens/{primitive,theme,semantic,custom}/**`; generate CSS via `scripts/migrate-tokens.py` — do not hand-duplicate values
- Do not invent lab-only tokens (see D004); use Mode `base/*` semantics
- Preserve aliases and Light/Dark when present in Figma
- Gap-report before token architecture changes; Figma paths live in `tokens/mappings/`
- Log semantic meaning changes in `docs/decisions.md`

## shadcn / components

- shadcn is the code foundation, not visual truth — customize via our tokens and APIs
- Reuse or extend before adding a new component or variant
- Align Figma concepts with code props (variant, size, state, icon, loading, disabled)
- Document meaningful API changes

## Storybook

- Production components need stories: default, variants, sizes, hover/focus/disabled/loading, error, long content, a11y edges
- Verify in Storybook; screenshots alone are not enough
- Non-happy-path states are required when specified

## Accessibility

Preserve keyboard nav, visible focus, semantic HTML, accessible names, contrast, disabled semantics, target size, and Radix/shadcn a11y — do not strip it.
